1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:05,960
I lost, Roberto-san.

2
00:00:06,210 --> 00:00:09,840
Now I understand why the kids' team is number one in Brazil.

3
00:00:10,090 --> 00:00:13,470
They're all excellent, energetic players.

4
00:00:13,550 --> 00:00:15,140
Thank you very much.

5
00:00:15,970 --> 00:00:19,430
By the way, I think you have two more matches in France.

6
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:20,350
That's right.

7
00:00:22,310 --> 00:00:23,480
You...

8
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:25,190
Hello.

9
00:01:56,430 --> 00:02:02,940
Episode 13: A Promise Under the Starry Sky

10
00:01:57,520 --> 00:02:00,020
I asked the French Football Federation and found out right away.

11
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:06,900
The team of kids from São Paulo is in Paris for a tournament.

12
00:02:07,610 --> 00:02:11,200
You are the famous former striker of the Brazilian national team,

13
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:14,200
the Japanese-Brazilian Roberto Hongo.

14
00:02:14,370 --> 00:02:16,870
I won't let you deny it any longer.

15
00:02:18,210 --> 00:02:22,840
Please, don't tell Tsubasa I'm in Paris.

16
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:31,340
I have no right to see him again.

17
00:02:33,140 --> 00:02:37,560
But the truth is, I'm here right now because of Tsubasa.

18
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:41,650
I quit football out of fear of losing my eyesight.

19
00:02:41,730 --> 00:02:43,940
And I buried my pain in alcohol.

20
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:48,650
Tsubasa is the one who gave me the strength to come back to life.

21
00:02:49,150 --> 00:02:50,360
Catch, here it comes!

22
00:02:57,750 --> 00:03:01,040
Good, come on!

23
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:03,170
That ball spinning in the sky...

24
00:03:04,090 --> 00:03:07,170
Gave me hope for life.

25
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:09,970
Now take this.

26
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:13,180
Watch out, move.

27
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:21,350
He deflected my shot.

28
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:40,040
Wakabayashi-kun, I accept your challenge.

29
00:03:43,170 --> 00:03:46,420
Are... are you Ozora Tsubasa?

30
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:50,670
That's right, I'm Ozora Tsubasa.

31
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:52,680
Ozora Tsubasa.

32
00:03:53,430 --> 00:03:57,760
At that moment, that name was engraved in my heart.

33
00:03:57,850 --> 00:03:58,680
And...

34
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:01,930
He's flying!

35
00:04:10,610 --> 00:04:11,820
Let it be a goal!

36
00:04:15,870 --> 00:04:17,580
The ball still hasn't gone out!

37
00:04:20,410 --> 00:04:25,210
Normally I don't like to waste this, but this match is worth a bottle of whiskey!

38
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:37,010
That's it! That man is the former Brazilian national team striker, Roberto Hongo.

39
00:04:37,470 --> 00:04:39,560
This will decide the winner...

40
00:04:40,430 --> 00:04:42,060
This cross will decide!

41
00:04:58,780 --> 00:05:00,740
He did it, goal.

42
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:04,250
Tsubasa scored with the cross...

43
00:05:04,620 --> 00:05:06,500
Our meeting was destiny.

44
00:05:07,830 --> 00:05:12,090
Ozora Tsubasa-kun, I'm Roberto Hongo.

45
00:05:12,340 --> 00:05:13,340
Nice to meet you.

46
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:18,390
Roberto Hongo, I know you.

47
00:05:18,470 --> 00:05:20,300
I've watched a lot of your matches.

48
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:24,980
Thank you, I'm very happy to see you.

49
00:05:28,770 --> 00:05:30,900
He magically took the ball away from me.

50
00:05:47,250 --> 00:05:48,080
Watch out!

51
00:06:01,970 --> 00:06:03,350
What!?

52
00:06:10,650 --> 00:06:11,940
Goal!

53
00:06:12,110 --> 00:06:13,320
Amazing!

54
00:06:13,610 --> 00:06:14,820
Alright!

55
00:06:14,980 --> 00:06:15,900
What?

56
00:06:16,860 --> 00:06:17,820
Tsubasa?

57
00:06:22,030 --> 00:06:22,950
Impossible.

58
00:06:23,030 --> 00:06:24,330
What? Hey...

59
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:34,130
You were great, Tsubasa.

60
00:06:34,210 --> 00:06:35,130
Really?

61
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:36,130
Yes.

62
00:06:39,590 --> 00:06:41,430
Alright, again!

63
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:55,070
Come on!

64
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:00,150
Goal!

65
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:03,700
Great, that was magnificent!

66
00:07:04,950 --> 00:07:06,160
Was it a goal?

67
00:07:08,750 --> 00:07:10,500
Goal!

68
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:13,920
Hooray, Tsubasa!

69
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:21,970
You're amazing, Tsubasa.

70
00:07:22,050 --> 00:07:23,890
Ay, ay, ay.

71
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:32,520
I can say I taught Tsubasa everything I know.

72
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:35,190
But most importantly...

73
00:07:35,860 --> 00:07:36,730
Tsubasa.

74
00:07:36,820 --> 00:07:38,440
What is it, Roberto?

75
00:07:38,690 --> 00:07:39,690
Remember.

76
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:41,950
The ball is your friend.

77
00:07:45,490 --> 00:07:49,250
The ball waits to play with you.

78
00:07:50,620 --> 00:07:53,830
Is the ball your friend?

79
00:07:55,250 --> 00:07:58,050
Tsubasa progressed rapidly.

80
00:07:58,630 --> 00:08:00,420
That's why I...

81
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:06,600
I will personally train Tsubasa to become the number one footballer in the world.

82
00:08:06,970 --> 00:08:07,810
Roberto!

83
00:08:07,890 --> 00:08:10,890
So please let me take Tsubasa to Brazil.

84
00:08:13,350 --> 00:08:14,480
Tsubasa!

85
00:08:15,810 --> 00:08:17,150
Roberto.

86
00:08:17,570 --> 00:08:20,690
Is it true you can't play football anymore?

87
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:22,530
Yes.

88
00:08:22,610 --> 00:08:24,740
Can you really not play?

89
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:29,660
Yes, I can never stand on the field again.

90
00:08:34,670 --> 00:08:35,790
Roberto...

91
00:08:36,290 --> 00:08:38,630
Brazil is a football country, isn't it?

92
00:08:39,630 --> 00:08:45,300
That's right, everyone there loves football and lives by it.

93
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:49,680
Roberto, I'm going to Brazil.

94
00:08:50,390 --> 00:08:54,310
But in the end, you didn't take Tsubasa.

95
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:03,440
He got past him.

96
00:09:05,110 --> 00:09:09,030
Now only Tsubasa-kun and the empty Miwa goal remain.

97
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:13,910
This means Nankatsu wins!

98
00:09:19,290 --> 00:09:24,550
The ball tears the net and rises to the sky.

99
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:32,220
And the sound of the whistle signals the end of the match.

100
00:09:32,390 --> 00:09:33,730
Amazing, Tsubasa!

101
00:09:33,810 --> 00:09:35,690
We did it! We won!

102
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:38,020
We won!

103
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:45,070
Tsubasa, congratulations, I'm at a loss for words.

104
00:09:45,860 --> 00:09:48,950
You've grown again in this tournament.

105
00:09:50,030 --> 00:09:56,660
You've faced various opponents, learned from them, and defeated them all.

106
00:09:57,120 --> 00:10:03,050
And just as you promised me, you managed to win the national cup.

107
00:10:04,380 --> 00:10:08,800
But Tsubasa... I can't keep my promise to you.

108
00:10:09,340 --> 00:10:11,760
Winning the tournament means Brazil, Roberto.

109
00:10:13,850 --> 00:10:16,520
This is the moment of goodbye, Tsubasa.

110
00:10:20,150 --> 00:10:25,740
"Dear Tsubasa, forgive me, but I can't..."

111
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:28,320
"I can't take you with me to Brazil."

112
00:10:28,910 --> 00:10:33,370
"As you know, the condition of my eye, diagnosed by doctors as retinal detachment,"

113
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:36,200
"no longer allows me to play football."

114
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:41,290
"For someone like me who lives for football, it was a huge shock."

115
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,880
"But the one who gave me a reason to live..."

116
00:10:45,420 --> 00:10:47,590
"was you, Tsubasa."

117
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:52,260
"Your football talent and genius captivated me,"

118
00:10:52,510 --> 00:10:56,020
"and I wanted to train you to become the best footballer in the world."

119
00:10:57,520 --> 00:10:58,770
"But Tsubasa,"

120
00:10:59,190 --> 00:11:02,610
"in the end, I can't take you to Brazil."

121
00:11:03,690 --> 00:11:07,990
"If I do that, I would be breaking up the Ozora family,"

122
00:11:08,990 --> 00:11:11,530
"and a family should stay together."

123
00:11:13,370 --> 00:11:17,700
"Though that's not the real reason I'm not taking you with me."

124
00:11:18,750 --> 00:11:26,380
"Whatever the reason, I've quit professional football, and that made me a loser."

125
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:33,390
"I can't train someone just beginning their real football life."

126
00:11:47,570 --> 00:11:48,690
Roberto...

127
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:53,320
Roberto!

128
00:11:55,780 --> 00:11:56,990
Roberto!

129
00:12:02,670 --> 00:12:03,670
Roberto...

130
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:05,670
Why?

131
00:12:08,090 --> 00:12:10,670
Why did you leave alone?

132
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:13,260
Roberto!!

133
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:18,010
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

134
00:12:20,830 --> 00:12:22,950
Born: September 7, Height: 180 cm, Weight: 75 kg, Blood Type: O

135
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:29,540
Just as I thought, even without me, Tsubasa has progressed.

136
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:32,300
He truly is a genius.

137
00:12:33,970 --> 00:12:39,890
Earlier this year, some colleagues were talking about a football video from Japan.

138
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:42,520
This kid is extraordinary.

139
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:45,270
Yes, head and shoulders above the rest.

140
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:49,520
Roberto, you came just in time.

141
00:12:49,610 --> 00:12:53,530
This is Japan U-15, and he is very special.

142
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:02,290
I found this by chance.

143
00:13:02,370 --> 00:13:06,960
I researched about him and found out his dream is to become a professional in Brazil.

144
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:12,130
I couldn't hold back my tears.

145
00:13:13,590 --> 00:13:17,930
And yesterday, Tsubasa's progress surprised me once again.

146
00:13:19,470 --> 00:13:20,930
But Roberto-san...

147
00:13:21,010 --> 00:13:27,020
Tsubasa thinks there's another reason why you didn't take him to Brazil.

148
00:13:28,190 --> 00:13:32,070
He thinks it's because he wasn't good enough.

149
00:13:32,270 --> 00:13:36,900
In his mind, if he had all the skills needed to become a professional in Brazil,

150
00:13:36,990 --> 00:13:40,070
you would have taken him with you.

151
00:13:41,370 --> 00:13:44,410
So he set himself a goal.

152
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:47,580
To succeed and reach Brazilian national football,

153
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:52,210
he said he couldn't afford to lose during his three years of middle school.

154
00:13:52,590 --> 00:13:54,210
He told himself if he couldn't do that,

155
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:59,220
he wouldn't be good enough to become a professional in Brazil.

156
00:14:00,590 --> 00:14:03,550
Following the notebook you left behind...

157
00:14:08,230 --> 00:14:11,520
Tsubasa trained harder than anyone else.

158
00:14:16,030 --> 00:14:17,280
And...

159
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:22,870
This summer, Tsubasa managed to achieve this goal.

160
00:14:25,490 --> 00:14:26,700
In his three years of middle school,

161
00:14:27,330 --> 00:14:30,580
he didn't lose to anyone in any official match.

162
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:36,500
Having achieved the triple crown in Japan,

163
00:14:37,010 --> 00:14:41,050
Tsubasa will undoubtedly go to Brazil after middle school graduation.

164
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:43,010
Please,

165
00:14:43,510 --> 00:14:48,020
Tsubasa plans to go to Brazil, Roberto-san, I hope you'll be his coach.

166
00:14:48,140 --> 00:14:52,150
This time, make Tsubasa's dream come true.

167
00:14:57,030 --> 00:14:59,740
Argentina is winning overwhelmingly!

168
00:15:06,410 --> 00:15:09,080
5-0 against Italy!

169
00:15:10,870 --> 00:15:12,710
This...

170
00:15:13,670 --> 00:15:16,750
We struggled so much against them.

171
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:22,300
Even though Hernandez isn't playing...

172
00:15:25,890 --> 00:15:28,970
At the International Youth Football Tournament in France,

173
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:31,140
a talented genius is emerging.

174
00:15:31,390 --> 00:15:35,900
With 5 goals alone, he even surpasses the German Schneider.

175
00:15:35,980 --> 00:15:36,860
Juan...

176
00:15:36,940 --> 00:15:37,980
...Diaz.

177
00:15:38,190 --> 00:15:41,070
And not only does he score goals...

178
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:44,530
As a midfielder, he's a creative playmaker.

179
00:15:45,110 --> 00:15:48,620
This once-in-a-century Argentine football genius,

180
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:51,700
as a scorer, Juan Diaz!

181
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:54,210
We're now interviewing Juan.

182
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:57,960
In the Japan-Italy match, you saw Japan's number 10,

183
00:15:58,040 --> 00:16:01,880
dribbling past the Italians with a South American style?

184
00:16:02,550 --> 00:16:05,340
Seeing him, I thought I could do that too.

185
00:16:05,430 --> 00:16:08,100
Well, the reason I could score 5 goals

186
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:12,730
was because their goalkeeper was different from the one in the Japan match.

187
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:21,940
I couldn't play against Hernandez today.

188
00:16:22,030 --> 00:16:28,070
But I'm very eager to play against Japan's number 10.

189
00:16:29,410 --> 00:16:30,490
Tsubasa.

190
00:16:31,700 --> 00:16:33,200
Juan Diaz.

191
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:38,250
~Nankatsu - Shizuoka~

192
00:16:49,260 --> 00:16:50,680
Sorry, I kept you waiting.

193
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:52,810
The Italy match again?

194
00:16:52,890 --> 00:16:54,020
Yes.

195
00:16:54,270 --> 00:16:57,230
I guess I always love watching it.

196
00:16:57,310 --> 00:16:59,770
Well, Misaki-kun is playing too.

197
00:16:59,860 --> 00:17:02,780
Did you tell him you watch his matches?

198
00:17:03,190 --> 00:17:04,240
Yes.

199
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:06,240
What did he say?

200
00:17:06,320 --> 00:17:09,780
Nothing, just thanked me for the support.

201
00:17:10,030 --> 00:17:13,200
Ah... he's not going to make a move.

202
00:17:13,910 --> 00:17:16,580
Next is against Argentina, right?

203
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:19,790
Yes, I think they are very strong.

204
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:22,800
You don't look worried at all.

205
00:17:23,130 --> 00:17:24,550
It's fine.

206
00:17:24,630 --> 00:17:26,550
Tsubasa-kun will win!

207
00:17:31,890 --> 00:17:33,060
Coach Mikami.

208
00:17:34,850 --> 00:17:39,440
Do you have any comments about the Argentina match?

209
00:17:39,650 --> 00:17:43,070
Well, I don't know what to say...

210
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:45,820
Coach!

211
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:48,860
All the kids have disappeared!

212
00:17:48,950 --> 00:17:50,570
What? Disappeared?

213
00:17:50,740 --> 00:17:53,580
None of them are in their rooms.

214
00:17:53,830 --> 00:17:54,950
What!?

215
00:18:06,010 --> 00:18:09,010
Juan Diaz from Argentina.

216
00:18:09,090 --> 00:18:12,600
As Tsubasa said, the world is a big place.

217
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:15,220
Every day we see new amazing players.

218
00:18:15,560 --> 00:18:19,890
We only knew Japan, that small place, and it was holding back our progress.

219
00:18:19,980 --> 00:18:24,570
Yes, coming to the cradle of football, Europe, really taught us that.

220
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:30,490
Our first tournament match was against Hamburg.

221
00:18:31,530 --> 00:18:36,240
That match made me realize how unskilled we were.

222
00:18:37,040 --> 00:18:39,250
Karl Heinz Schneider.

223
00:18:42,460 --> 00:18:45,670
He showed us how many great players there are in the world.

224
00:18:46,590 --> 00:18:52,970
We seriously thought we could win without Tsubasa.

225
00:18:53,090 --> 00:18:55,510
And then, the second match against Bremen.

226
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:59,980
We couldn't control Schester in midfield.

227
00:19:00,850 --> 00:19:05,310
But we all trained harder because of that defeat.

228
00:19:05,570 --> 00:19:06,520
Misugi.

229
00:19:07,690 --> 00:19:11,360
We've come this far and there's no turning back.

230
00:19:11,530 --> 00:19:12,780
Hyuga.

231
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:15,950
Now we've moved forward.

232
00:19:16,450 --> 00:19:19,500
Exactly, we're heading toward the top of the world.

233
00:19:19,580 --> 00:19:21,540
No turning back.

234
00:19:23,170 --> 00:19:26,000
We always used to fight against Tsubasa.

235
00:19:26,090 --> 00:19:28,460
But now we've formed a united team.

236
00:19:28,550 --> 00:19:31,920
No matter how tough it gets, this team can reach the top.

237
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:34,340
We can beat the world!

238
00:19:34,430 --> 00:19:36,220
Yes!

239
00:19:36,350 --> 00:19:40,680
Tonight, everyone's dream and goal became one.

240
00:19:41,100 --> 00:19:44,190
Tsubasa has been dreaming of this goal since childhood.

241
00:19:44,270 --> 00:19:50,190
A goal where Japan wins and is at the top of the world.

242
00:19:50,650 --> 00:19:55,950
And now, he had friends who share the same dream and goal, striving for it.

243
00:19:56,280 --> 00:19:58,330
This made Tsubasa happy.

244
00:20:00,830 --> 00:20:03,710
So to make Japan number one in the world,

245
00:20:04,170 --> 00:20:08,000
let's win this tournament, guys.

246
00:20:08,090 --> 00:20:09,210
Okay!

247
00:20:09,590 --> 00:20:14,220
There are elite and great players, but we're after this cup!

248
00:20:14,680 --> 00:20:17,970
Yes, the final is against Germany, we have to settle the score with them.

249
00:20:18,350 --> 00:20:21,720
Tsubasa, to get there, we first play Argentina.

250
00:20:22,390 --> 00:20:27,270
Will Tsubasa or Diaz control the midfield? That will decide the winner.

251
00:20:28,650 --> 00:20:31,980
It's a duel against the genius Juan Diaz, Tsubasa.

252
00:20:35,570 --> 00:20:38,990
Where did they go? It's so late.

253
00:20:40,370 --> 00:20:41,660
Coach!

254
00:20:48,130 --> 00:20:49,250
Guys.

255
00:20:49,340 --> 00:20:50,920
What's up?

256
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:55,510
Coach, we want to win again tomorrow!

257
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:59,720
It's time to show the results of our hard work.

258
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:02,060
You just have to wait and watch, right?

259
00:21:02,140 --> 00:21:03,140
Right.

260
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:06,520
If we beat Argentina, we go to the final.

261
00:21:06,810 --> 00:21:10,520
And finally beat Germany and lift the cup.

262
00:21:11,110 --> 00:21:13,280
Let's do this, coach.

263
00:21:28,670 --> 00:21:30,540
Cannon Shot!

264
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:39,390
Yes.

265
00:21:40,680 --> 00:21:44,390
Napoleon from France is chasing Germany's Schneider.

266
00:21:44,470 --> 00:21:46,810
He scores his second hat-trick.

